From fda6603f3520d95339d3b3d8b2e3c96a62f0c97b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ada <ada@6bit.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 17:55:26 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] runtime: shim-owned swtpm for seed TPM sandboxes

Sandboxes annotated with seed.loom.farm/tpm-mode (create|verify) get one
swtpm owned by the shim, managed like virtiofsd. Before cloud-hypervisor
starts, the shim:

1. checks that swtpm_sentinel_path contains swtpm_expected_fsid, and
   that the state dir is below the sentinel's dir on the same filesystem
2. takes an exclusive flock on <state-dir>/.session-lock (up to
   swtpm_lock_timeout); the lock fd is shared with swtpm so the lock is
   held for as long as swtpm lives
3. starts swtpm (seed:// backend, startup-clear, ctrl socket in the
   sandbox dir, per-sandbox volatile dir, SWTPM_SEED_ALLOW_CREATE=1 only
   in create mode) with Pdeathsig on a locked OS thread and its own
   process group; create mode refuses an existing permall
4. computes the TPM fingerprint over the swtpm ctrl + data channels:
   SHA-256 of the marshaled TPMT_PUBLIC of the owner-hierarchy ECC P-256
   SRK (TCG template, unique = 32+32 zero bytes)
5. create: writes <state-dir>/tpm-fingerprint atomically; verify:
   compares with seed.loom.farm/tpm-fingerprint
6. closes its data channel and syncs on the ctrl channel so swtpm has
   dropped the data fd before CLH sends CMD_SET_DATAFD; CLH's own
   CMD_STOP/CMD_INIT then power-cycles the TPM

swtpm dying after boot stops the VM (CLH never reconnects). On teardown
swtpm gets SIGTERM, then SIGKILL, and only then is the lock released and
the volatile dir and socket removed. The legacy tpm_socket annotation is
unchanged; the two are mutually exclusive.

New config keys (hypervisor.clh): swtpm_path, swtpm_sentinel_path,
swtpm_expected_fsid, swtpm_lock_timeout.

TPM2 marshaling (CreatePrimary, FlushContext, Startup) is implemented
inline; kata vendors no TPM library.

Co-Authored-By: Joshua Perry <josh@6bit.com>
